## Auth System

Session is in-memory React state only — resets on page refresh (no localStorage).

### Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `client/contexts/AuthContext.tsx` | `Account` type, pre-seeded accounts, `AuthProvider`, `useAuth()` |
| `client/components/auth/SignInScreen.tsx` | Full-page account picker shown when `activeAccount === null` |
| `client/components/auth/ProfileMenu.tsx` | Dropdown from avatar: current user, other accounts, settings, sign out |
| `client/components/auth/SettingsPanel.tsx` | Settings panel (24h / week start) extracted from TopBar |

### AuthContext API


interface Account {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  initials: string;
  color: string;  // hex, unique per account
}

const { activeAccount, accounts, signIn, signOut, switchAccount } = useAuth();
```

Pre-seeded accounts: `alex-personal` (gmail) and `alex-work` (acme.co).

### App Shell Gate

`client/App.tsx` wraps everything in `<AuthProvider>`. `AppShell` reads `activeAccount` — renders `<SignInScreen>` when null, otherwise the normal routes.

### TopBar Integration

Avatar button is in the rightmost slot of TopBar, inside a relative-positioned `avatarAreaRef` div. It opens `<ProfileMenu>` or `<SettingsPanel>` as absolute dropdowns within that container.

- ProfileMenu handles its own click-outside via `useEffect + mousedown`
- SettingsPanel click-outside is handled in TopBar via `avatarAreaRef`
- Avatar shows active account's `initials` and `color`; has `aria-label="Account"` and a 2px primary border ring when open

### Events & Preferences

Calendar events and preferences are **shared across accounts** (no per-account isolation). Switching accounts only changes which initials/color appear in the avatar.
